	          <li><span class="ck ck-ic"><svg class="pic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15.39 4.39a1 1 0 0 0 1.68-.474 2.5 2.5 0 1 1 3.014 3.015 1 1 0 0 0-.474 1.68l1.683 1.682a2.414 2.414 0 0 1 0 3.414L19.61 15.39a1 1 0 0 1-1.68-.474 2.5 2.5 0 1 0-3.014 3.015 1 1 0 0 1 .474 1.68l-1.683 1.682a2.414 2.414 0 0 1-3.414 0L8.61 19.61a1 1 0 0 0-1.68.474 2.5 2.5 0 1 1-3.014-3.015 1 1 0 0 0 .474-1.68l-1.683-1.682a2.414 2.414 0 0 1 0-3.414L4.39 8.61a1 1 0 0 1 1.68.474 2.5 2.5 0 1 0 3.014-3.015 1 1 0 0 1-.474-1.68l1.683-1.682a2.414 2.414 0 0 1 3.414 0z"/></svg></span><span><strong>Integrations:</strong> enable another plugin for an agent and it can call that plugin's API directly. Dataview, Tasks and TaskNotes come with ready skills, Canvas and Bases files are read and written with the normal tools, and any plugin exposing an API is picked up automatically.</span></li>
	        </ul>
	        <p class="fmore fmore-left">
	          Also: MCP servers, image and PDF attachments, subagents with their
	          own instructions, and several chats running in parallel.
	        </p>
	      </div>
	      {/* A static chat still — like the search still it runs no JS and reuses
	          the demo's own classes (.v-chat, .msg, .act, .msg-ai, .pcb, the
	          composer), so it cannot drift from the demo window. Every activity
	          line is a real tool summary: label + ", " + outcome, past tense once
	          done (toolSummaryModel.ts — "Loaded skill <name>", "Searched notes
	          for “q”, found N notes", "Read <note>, N lines"), and every action
	          the agent takes has one: consecutive same-tool calls merge into a
	          single row, and the staged edit shows the manage_notes call that
	          staged it rather than appearing on its own. The story is not
	          the demo's: a different ask, different notes, and the skill load
	          on show because Skills is a point beside it. The staged edit is an
	          Update (the only badge the site styles) with the real bar's count
	          wording. Ids are omitted — the demo's composer owns them. */}
